                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "lazy mobile port that only runs in a tiny fixed window that was already a problem 12 years ago when the game came out on pc, and it's an ever-increasing issue as monitors and resolutions go bigger and higher. there's a thin (480x640) and wide (1024x640) option, wide only adds more background on top.\n\ndecent pixel graphics, music provided by kevin macleod. separate volumes, zen and pro difficulty and a colorblind toggle are the only settings, with only volumes and thin/wide available while playing. there's a how to play section, a monster library (just icons of encountered ones, no names or info), a stats screen and some non-rebindable hotkeys.\n\n[b]mousing and typing and general keyboard navigation both work (navigation to a lesser extent)[/b], which is always a pleasant surprise in any word game, especially mobile ports. [b]it's not turn-based[/b] though, so the best strategy is spamming 3-letter words. brush up on those, check the rest of your vocabulary at the door and you're golden. endless shuffles on offer but the only time words are defined is during events, when they're used to open a chest or fully heal a hero when they're about to die. there are also traps to disarm by removing as many letters as possible to minimize damage.\n\n19 heroes to unlock and tediously level by replaying 6 stages over and over. once unlocked, any stage can be replayed, don't need to start at the beginning, and you're running parties of 3, so it's not individual grind, but after 6 hours (the in-game timer is more accurate, steam's runtime indicator is just that), I've only maxed out 2 heroes, 2 are still locked, along with 5 of the 84 monsters.\n\nit does some things right and it's fun for a while in a mindless way (whatever's happening on top is irrelevant, just keep submitting words), the 3 eur price is fine too. [b]it sort of saves mid-run progress on exit[/b], meaning whether you quit during a battle or right before, [b]you'll be faced with a random new enemy next time[/b]. I guess it only saves the encounter number, but also loot and hero stats until then, so why not do it properly? either way, [b]without full screen and better text display options it has to be a thumbs down[/b].",
